# Fix "Meta Device" Loading Error — Revised (RAM-Safe)

## Problem

The previous plan scanned all 11 Gemma shards (~48GB) for a few MB of projector keys. Combined with the 24GB `from_pretrained` backbone load, peak RAM exceeded 64GB and nearly crashed the PC.

## Root Cause Analysis

The text encoder requires weights from **two separate sources**:

| Weight Keys | Located In | Size |
|---|---|---|
| `multi_modal_projector.mm_input_projection_weight` | Gemma [text_encoder/model-00001-of-00011.safetensors](file:///c:/just-dub-it/weights/gemma/text_encoder/model-00001-of-00011.safetensors) | ~9 MB |
| `multi_modal_projector.mm_soft_emb_norm.weight` | Gemma [text_encoder/model-00001-of-00011.safetensors](file:///c:/just-dub-it/weights/gemma/text_encoder/model-00001-of-00011.safetensors) | ~5 KB |
| `model.diffusion_model.video_embeddings_connector.*` | Main `ltx-2-19b-dev.safetensors` | ~200 MB |
| `model.diffusion_model.audio_embeddings_connector.*` | Main `ltx-2-19b-dev.safetensors` | ~200 MB |
| `text_embedding_projection.aggregate_embed.weight` | Main `ltx-2-19b-dev.safetensors` | ~720 MB (old, unused) |
| Full Gemma backbone | Loaded via `from_pretrained()` | ~24 GB (bfloat16) |

> [!CAUTION]
> The builder was given ALL 11 shards but only shard 1 has matching keys. Shards 2-11 contain only Gemma backbone weights which are already loaded separately by `from_pretrained`. Opening and scanning 48GB of files is unnecessary.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] [model_ledger.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-pipelines/src/ltx_pipelines/model_ledger.py)

**Split the `text_encoder_builder` into two builders** that load from the correct source:

1. **`text_encoder_projector_builder`**: Loads from **shard 1 only** of the Gemma text_encoder directory. Maps `multi_modal_projector.*` → `feature_extractor_linear.*`.
2. **`text_encoder_connector_builder`**: Loads from the **main LTX checkpoint**. Maps `model.diffusion_model.*_embeddings_connector.*` → `embeddings_connector.*` / `audio_embeddings_connector.*`.

Override [text_encoder()](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-pipelines/src/ltx_pipelines/model_ledger.py#248-256) to:
1. Build the meta model on meta device
2. Load projector weights from shard 1 (~9 MB)
3. Load connector weights from main checkpoint (~400 MB)
4. Apply [module_ops](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/text_encoders/gemma/encoders/base_encoder.py#252-279) (loads 24 GB Gemma backbone via `from_pretrained`)
5. Validate no params remain on meta device

**Peak RAM**: ~24 GB (Gemma backbone) + ~400 MB (connectors) + ~9 MB (projector) + OS ≈ **~26 GB** (well within 64 GB).

### [MODIFY] [av_encoder.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/text_encoders/gemma/encoders/av_encoder.py)

Split `AV_GEMMA_TEXT_ENCODER_KEY_OPS` into two separate [SDOps](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/loader/sd_ops.py#64-119):
- `AV_GEMMA_PROJECTOR_KEY_OPS` — matches/maps `multi_modal_projector.*`
- `AV_GEMMA_CONNECTOR_KEY_OPS` — matches/maps `model.diffusion_model.*_connector.*`

### Already Done (kept from previous plan)
- [GemmaFeaturesExtractorLightricks](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/text_encoders/gemma/feature_extractor.py#46-99) already created in [feature_extractor.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/text_encoders/gemma/feature_extractor.py) ✅
- [AVGemmaTextEncoderModelConfigurator](file:///c:/just-dub-it/packages/ltx-core/src/ltx_core/text_encoders/gemma/encoders/av_encoder.py#74-85) already updated to use it ✅

